Note on assets: the 3D models, textures, audio and font used by the app come
from the same upstream repository. This repository does NOT contain or
redistribute them: scripts/fetch-assets.mjs downloads them locally from the
pinned revision above, and apps/desktop/public/assets/ is gitignored.

The upstream README states that its game assets are used for educational
purposes under a fair-use rationale and that its author is not associated with
Hipster Whale, the makers of the original Crossy Road. The MIT license above
covers the upstream source code; it does not by itself grant rights to the
original game's branding or art. Release builds and the web bundle embed the
assets, so do not distribute them without replacing the assets and the name.

